{"actor":"erik","body":"{\"ac_map\":[{\"parent_ac\":\"AC1 TestBenchMainRedirectsExecutionSubcommands\",\"coverage\":\"A3d AC1\"},{\"parent_ac\":\"AC2 test_sigterm_marks_interrupted_and_stops_containers\",\"coverage\":\"A3b AC1\"},{\"parent_ac\":\"AC3 test_sigint_same_behavior\",\"coverage\":\"A3b AC2\"},{\"parent_ac\":\"AC4 test_concurrency_group_flock_serializes\",\"coverage\":\"A3a AC1\"},{\"parent_ac\":\"AC5 test_in_flight_json_tracks_cells\",\"coverage\":\"A3a AC2\"},{\"parent_ac\":\"AC6 test_max_cost_usd_produces_budget_halted\",\"coverage\":\"A3c AC1\"},{\"parent_ac\":\"AC7 test_budget_json_accumulates\",\"coverage\":\"A3c AC2\"},{\"parent_ac\":\"AC8 fiz-bench matrix shell redirect\",\"coverage\":\"A3d AC3\"}],\"child_ids\":[\"fizeau-c72424e8\",\"fizeau-86f2bac0\",\"fizeau-2b192ca5\",\"fizeau-0ee8d176\"],\"rationale\":\"Split along four orthogonal runtime concerns from the parent's PROPOSED FIX list: (A3a) concurrency primitives — flock, --jobs pool, in-flight.json; (A3b) signal hygiene — trap/setsid/docker label cleanup/interrupted reports; (A3c) cost enforcement — pricing tally, budget.json, budget_halted placeholder; (A3d) Go-runner deactivation — cmd/bench redirect. Each child touches a distinct code surface (lock plumbing vs trap handler vs cost accumulator vs cmd/bench dispatch), can be tested independently with its own scripts/benchmark/test/ harness, and maps cleanly to a subset of the parent ACs. A3b references in-flight.json from A3a but only as a read input, so the two can land in either order with a small fallback (enumerate by jobs table) if A3a lands later. A3d is fully independent of the bash runner and can land first.\"}","created_at":"2026-05-17T21:01:55.414888695Z","kind":"triage-decomposed","source":"ddx work","summary":"decomposed into fizeau-c72424e8, fizeau-86f2bac0, fizeau-2b192ca5, fizeau-0ee8d176"}
